{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_35","type":"mcp_tool_call","server":"fetch","tool":"fetch","arguments":{"max_length":12000,"start_index":10000,"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2023_in_China"},"result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Contents of https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2023_in_China:\nafter [Typhon Haikui](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2023_Pacific_typhoon_season#Typhoon_Haikui_(Hanna) \"2023 Pacific typhoon season\") makes [landfall](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Landfall \"Landfall\") over the region. Rainfall in [Shenzhen](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shenzhen \"Shenzhen\") reaches record levels, the heaviest since meteorological records began in the city.[[17]](#cite_note-17)\n* 22 September – [Syrian President](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/President_of_Syria \"President of Syria\") [Bashar al-Assad](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bashar_al-Assad \"Bashar al-Assad\") visits China, meets with [Chinese leader](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paramount_leader \"Paramount leader\") [Xi Jinping](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Xi_Jinping \"Xi Jinping\"), and signs a strategic partnership with China on infrastructure as part of China's [Belt and Road Initiative](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Belt_and_Road_Initiative \"Belt and Road Initiative\").[[18]](#cite_note-18)\n* 13 October – An [Israeli](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Israel \"Israel\") [diplomat](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Diplomat \"Diplomat\") based at the [Embassy of Israel, Beijing](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Embassy_of_Israel,_Beijing \"Embassy of Israel, Beijing\") is stabbed by an unknown foreign attacker. The diplomat was taken to a hospital for treatment and is in stable condition. The incident is being treated as a [terrorist](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Terrorism_in_China \"Terrorism in China\") attack.[[19]](#cite_note-19)\n* 16 October\n  + China will provide emergency [humanitarian aid](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Humanitarian_aid \"Humanitarian aid\") to the [UN Palestine agency](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/UNRWA \"UNRWA\") and the [Palestinian Authority](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Palestinian_Authority \"Palestinian Authority\"). The [CIDCA](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/China_International_Development_Cooperation_Agency \"China International Development Cooperation Agency\") says the aid will be used to address urgent needs, such as food and medical care.[[20]](#cite_note-20)\n  + Former [Bank of China](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bank_of_China \"Bank of China\") chair [Liu Lian'ge](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Liu_Lian'ge \"Liu Lian'ge\") is arrested on allegations of [corruption](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Corruption_in_China \"Corruption in China\").[[21]](#cite_note-21)\n* 17 October – [Hungarian Prime Minister](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Prime_Minister_of_Hungary \"Prime Minister of Hungary\") [Viktor Orbán](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Viktor_Orb%C3%A1n \"Viktor Orbán\") and [Russian President](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/President_of_Russia \"President of Russia\") [Vladimir Putin](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vladimir_Putin \"Vladimir Putin\") hold [talks](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Diplomacy \"Diplomacy\") at the Belt and Road Initiative forum in Beijing. It is the first meeting between Putin and an [EU](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/European_Union \"European Union\") leader since [Russia's invasion of Ukraine](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Russian_invasion_of_Ukraine \"Russian invasion of Ukraine\").[[22]](#cite_note-22)\n* 24 October – The [Standing Committee of the National People's Congress of China](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Standing_Committee_of_the_National_People's_Congress_of_China \"Standing Committee of the National People's Congress of China\") votes to remove several [SCtate Council](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/State_Council_of_China \"State Council of China\") members from their positions, including [defense minister](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Minister_of_National_Defense_(China) \"Minister of National Defense (China)\") [Li Shangfu](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Li_Shangfu \"Li Shangfu\"), [finance minister](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ministry_of_Finance_(China) \"Ministry of Finance (China)\") [Liu Kun](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Liu_Kun \"Liu Kun\"), and [science minister](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ministry_of_Science_and_Technology_(China) \"Ministry of Science and Technology (China)\") [Wang Zhigang](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wang_Zhigang \"Wang Zhigang\").[[23]](#cite_note-23)\n* 10 November – China imposes \"control measures\" against [Philippine](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Philippine \"Philippine\") vessels at a contested [South China Sea](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/South_China_Sea \"South China Sea\") location after a Philippine [auxiliary ship](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Auxiliary_ship \"Auxiliary ship\") entered the area which China deemed as infringing on its [sovereignty](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sovereignty \"Sovereignty\").[[24]](#cite_note-24)\n* 13 November – [2023 Chinese pneumonia outbreak](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2023_Chinese_pneumonia_outbreak \"2023 Chinese pneumonia outbreak\"): [National Health Commission](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/National_Health_Commission \"National Health Commission\") reports a [pneumonia](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pneumonia \"Pneumonia\") outbreak in Beijing and Liaoning.[[25]](#cite_note-25)\n* 15 November – [U.S. President](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/President_of_the_United_States \"President of the United States\") [Joe Biden](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Joe_Biden \"Joe Biden\") and Xi Jinping hold talks in [San Francisco](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/San_Francisco \"San Francisco\"), [California](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/California \"California\"), United States, their first meeting in over a year. The talks are described as being positive with \"real progress\" being made on key issues such as [drug trafficking](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Illegal_drug_trade \"Illegal drug trade\") and [artificial intelligence](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Artificial_intelligence \"Artificial intelligence\").[[26]](#cite_note-26)\n* 16 November – [Lüliang office fire](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/L%C3%BCliang_office_fire?action=edit&redlink=1 \"Lüliang office fire (page does not exist)\"): At least 26 people are killed and 63 were hospitalized by a fire at the Yongju Coal Industry Joint Building in [Lüliang](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/L%C3%BCliang \"Lüliang\"), [Shanxi](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shanxi \"Shanxi\").[[27]](#cite_note-27)\n* 21 November – The [Chinese Foreign Ministry](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chinese_Foreign_Ministry \"Chinese Foreign Ministry\") warns [Argentina](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Argentina \"Argentina\") against severing ties as a \"serious mistake\", after [president](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/President_of_Argentina \"President of Argentina\")-elect [Javier Milei](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Javier_Milei \"Javier Milei\") vowed to do so.[[28]](#cite_note-28)\n* 27 November – A [Chinese court](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Judicial_system_of_China \"Judicial system of China\") commences [compensation](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Financial_compensation \"Financial compensation\") hearings for the Chinese relatives of passengers on [Malaysia Airlines Flight 370](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Malaysia_Airlines_Flight_370 \"Malaysia Airlines Flight 370\").[[29]](#cite_note-29)\n* 6 December – [Archaeologists](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Archaeology \"Archaeology\") discover an ancient [Han dynasty](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Han_dynasty \"Han dynasty\") tomb.[[30]](#cite_note-30)\n* 14 December – [2023 Beijing Subway collision](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2023_Beijing_Subway_collision \"2023 Beijing Subway collision\"): At least 515 people are injured in a [rear-end collision](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rear-end_collision \"Rear-end collision\") between [railroad cars](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Railroad_car \"Railroad car\") on the [Beijing Subway](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beijing_Subway \"Beijing Subway\") near the [Xi'erqi station](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Xi'erqi_station \"Xi'erqi station\") amid snowfall.[[31]](#cite_note-31)\n* 16 December\n  + The [China Meteorological Administration](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/China_Meteorological_Administration \"China Meteorological Administration\") issues a [low-temperature warning](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Weather_warning \"Weather warning\"), [forecasting](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Weather_forecasting \"Weather forecasting\") a [cold wave](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cold_wave \"Cold wave\") affecting most of the country.[[32]](#cite_note-32)\n  + A [court](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Judicial_system_of_China \"Judicial system of China\") in [Baiyin](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Baiyin \"Baiyin\"), [Gansu](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gansu \"Gansu\") [sentences](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sentence_(law) \"Sentence (law)\") five organizers of a 2021 [ultramarathon](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ultramarathon \"Ultramarathon\") to prison terms ranging from three to five and a half years, following the [deaths of 21 runners](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gansu_ultramarathon_disaster \"Gansu ultramarathon disaster\") due to [extreme weather](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cold_front \"Cold front\") during the event.[[33]](#cite_note-33)\n* 18 December\n  + [Serial killer](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Serial_killer \"Serial killer\") [Lao Rongzhi](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lao_Rongzhi \"Lao Rongzhi\") is [executed](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Capital_punishment_in_China \"Capital punishment in China\") for the [murders](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Murder_in_Chinese_law \"Murder in Chinese law\") of seven people between 1996 and 1999.[[34]](#cite_note-34)\n  + [2023 Jishishan earthquake](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2023_Jishishan_earthquake \"2023 Jishishan earthquake\"): At least 127 people are killed by a magnitude 6.2 [earthquake](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Earthquake \"Earthquake\") in Gansu and [Qinghai](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Qinghai \"Qinghai\"). Over 700 others are injured.[[35]](#cite_note-35)[[36]](#cite_note-36) It is China's deadliest earthquake in years.[[37]](#cite_note-37)\n* 20 December – Twelve people are killed and 13 others injured when a [mining](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mining \"Mining\") cart runs off the tracks in [Jixi](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jixi \"Jixi\"), [Heilongjiang](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Heilongjiang \"Heilongjiang\").[[38]](#cite_note-38)\n* 22 December – China passes a series of regulations aimed at limiting video game [microtransactions](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Microtransaction \"Microtransaction\"). The new rules include banning rewards for logging on for multiple consecutive days and banning rewards for players if they spend money in a game for the first time.[[39]](#cite_note-39)\n* 29 December – The [National People's Congress of China](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/National_People's_Congress_of_China \"National People's Congress of China\") appoints commander of the [People's Liberation Army Navy](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/People's_Liberation_Army_Navy \"People's Liberation Army Navy\") [Dong Jun](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dong_Jun \"Dong Jun\") as the [Minister of National Defense](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Minister_of_National_Defense_(China) \"Minister of National Defense (China)\"), succeeding [Li Shangfu](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Li_Shangfu \"Li Shangfu\").[[40]](#cite_note-40)\n\n|  |  |\n| --- | --- |\n|  | This section needs to be **updated**. Please help update this article to reflect recent events or newly available information. *(November 2023)* |\n\n* 1 January\n  + [Wei Lian](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wei_Lian?action=edit&redlink=1 \"Wei Lian (page does not exist)\"), 77, [film director](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Film_director \"Film director\").[[41]](#cite_note-41)\n  + [Fan Weitang](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fan_Weitang \"Fan Weitang\"), 87, mining engineer.[[42]](#cite_note-42)\n  + [Zhu Zushou](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zhu_Zushou \"Zhu Zushou\"), 77, [diplomat](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Diplomat \"Diplomat\"), [ambassador](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ambassador \"Ambassador\") to [Hungary](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_ambassadors_of_China_to_Hungary \"List of ambassadors of Chin\n\n<error>Content truncated. Call the fetch tool with a start_index of 22000 to get more content.</error>"}],"structured_content":null},"error":null,"status":"completed"}}
