{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_50","type":"mcp_tool_call","server":"fetch","tool":"fetch","arguments":{"max_length":8000,"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/China%E2%80%93Russia_relations"},"result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Contents of https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/China%E2%80%93Russia_relations:\nChina–Russia relations\n\n|  |  |\n| --- | --- |\n| [Map indicating locations of China and Russia](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:China_Russia_Locator_3D.svg \"Map indicating locations of China and Russia\") | |\n|  | |\n|  |  |\n| [China](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/China \"China\") | [Russia](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Russia \"Russia\") |\n| Diplomatic mission | |\n| [Chinese Embassy, Moscow](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Embassy_of_China,_Moscow \"Embassy of China, Moscow\") | [Russian Embassy, Beijing](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Embassy_of_Russia,_Beijing \"Embassy of Russia, Beijing\") |\n| Envoy | |\n| [Ambassador](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_ambassadors_of_China_to_Russia \"List of ambassadors of China to Russia\") [Zhang Hanhui](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zhang_Hanhui \"Zhang Hanhui\") | [Ambassador](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_ambassadors_of_Russia_to_China \"List of ambassadors of Russia to China\") [Igor Morgulov](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Igor_Morgulov \"Igor Morgulov\") |\n\n[![](//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a5/Xi_Jinping_and_Vladimir_Putin.jpg/330px-Xi_Jinping_and_Vladimir_Putin.jpg)](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Xi_Jinping_and_Vladimir_Putin.jpg)\n\n[Russian president](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/President_of_Russia \"President of Russia\") [Vladimir Putin](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vladimir_Putin \"Vladimir Putin\") with [Chinese leader](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paramount_leader \"Paramount leader\") [Xi Jinping](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Xi_Jinping \"Xi Jinping\") during a [state visit](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_international_trips_made_by_Xi_Jinping \"List of international trips made by Xi Jinping\") to [Moscow](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Moscow \"Moscow\") for the [2025 Victory Day Parade](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2025_Moscow_Victory_Day_Parade \"2025 Moscow Victory Day Parade\"), May 2025\n\n\n\nChina and Russia share one of the world's most important foreign relationships.[[a]](#cite_note-2) Both nations share interest in energy cooperation, military ties, and geopolitical alignment in challenging the collective West at large, including the United States.\n\n[Relations](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/History_of_Sino-Russian_relations \"History of Sino-Russian relations\") between China and Russia go back to the 16th century. Though initially allies during the [Cold War](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cold_War \"Cold War\"), [China and the Soviet Union](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sino-Soviet_relations \"Sino-Soviet relations\") were rivals after the [Sino-Soviet split](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sino-Soviet_split \"Sino-Soviet split\") in 1961. After the [dissolution of the Soviet Union](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dissolution_of_the_Soviet_Union \"Dissolution of the Soviet Union\") in 1991, China and Russia established diplomatic relations, with the relationship strengthening significantly afterwards. The two countries share a land border which was [demarcated in 1991](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1991_Sino-Soviet_Border_Agreement \"1991 Sino-Soviet Border Agreement\"), and they signed the [Treaty of Good-Neighborliness and Friendly Cooperation](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2001_Sino-Russian_Treaty_of_Friendship \"2001 Sino-Russian Treaty of Friendship\") in 2001. Ties grew closer following [international sanctions against Russia](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/International_sanctions_during_the_Russo-Ukrainian_war \"International sanctions during the Russo-Ukrainian war\") for its [2014 annexation of Crimea](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2014_Russian_annexation_of_Crimea \"2014 Russian annexation of Crimea\"), which led Russia to pursue a pivot to China; in that year, China and Russia signed a 30-year gas deal worth $400 billion. In 2019, the two countries defined their relationship as a \"[comprehensive strategic partnership of coordination for a new era](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_diplomatic_partnerships_of_China \"List of diplomatic partnerships of China\").\" Ties have continued to deepen since the start of the [Russo-Ukrainian war](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Russo-Ukrainian_war_(2022%E2%80%93present) \"Russo-Ukrainian war (2022–present)\") in 2022, with Russia increasingly becoming dependent on China while it is under [large-scale international sanctions](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/International_sanctions_during_the_Russian_invasion_of_Ukraine \"International sanctions during the Russian invasion of Ukraine\"). China and Russia have significant economic ties, and Russia is an important source of natural energy and oil for China, while China is a critical source of consumer and industrial goods for Russia. China is by far Russia's largest trading partner. The annual trade between China and Russia was US$234 billion as of 2025.\n\nChina and Russia have enjoyed close relations militarily, economically, and politically, while supporting each other on various global issues. Commentators have debated whether the bilateral strategic partnership constitutes an alliance. China and Russia officially declared their relations \"Not allies, but better than allies\". The two countries cooperate through multilateral organizations and project such as the [Shanghai Cooperation Organisation](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shanghai_Cooperation_Organisation \"Shanghai Cooperation Organisation\"), [BRICS](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/BRICS \"BRICS\") and the [Belt and Road Initiative](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Belt_and_Road_Initiative \"Belt and Road Initiative\"). Russia recognizes [Taiwan](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Taiwan \"Taiwan\") as an integral part of China, and supports [Chinese unification](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chinese_unification \"Chinese unification\"). Russia also supports China's policies in [Hong Kong](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hong_Kong \"Hong Kong\"), [Tibet](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tibet_Autonomous_Region \"Tibet Autonomous Region\") and [Xinjiang](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Xinjiang \"Xinjiang\"). In turn, China has called for Russia's security concerns to be accounted for and has opposed the [enlargement of NATO](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Enlargement_of_NATO \"Enlargement of NATO\") and sanctions against Russia.\n\nThe relations between China and Russia go back to the 16th century, when the [Qing dynasty](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Qing_dynasty \"Qing dynasty\") tried to drive Russian settlers out of [Manchuria](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Manchuria \"Manchuria\"), ended by the signing of the [Treaty of Nerchinsk](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Treaty_of_Nerchinsk \"Treaty of Nerchinsk\"). The Russian Empire consolidated its control over the [Russian Far East](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Russian_Far_East \"Russian Far East\") in the 19th century, after the [annexation](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Amur_Annexation \"Amur Annexation\") of part of Chinese Manchuria (1858–1860).[[2]](#cite_note-3)\n\nAfter the [establishment of the People's Republic of China](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Proclamation_of_the_People's_Republic_of_China \"Proclamation of the People's Republic of China\") in 1949, [China and the Soviet Union](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sino-Soviet_relations \"Sino-Soviet relations\") were initially allies. During the [Cold War](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cold_War \"Cold War\"), the two countries turned into rivals after the [Sino-Soviet split](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sino-Soviet_split \"Sino-Soviet split\") in 1961, competing for control of the worldwide Communist movement. There was a serious possibility of a major war between the two nations in the early 1960s; a brief [border war took place in 1969](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sino-Soviet_border_conflict \"Sino-Soviet border conflict\"). This enmity began to lessen after the death of [Chairman of the Chinese Communist Party](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chairman_of_the_Chinese_Communist_Party \"Chairman of the Chinese Communist Party\") [Mao Zedong](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mao_Zedong \"Mao Zedong\") in \n\n<error>Content truncated. Call the fetch tool with a start_index of 8000 to get more content.</error>"}],"structured_content":null},"error":null,"status":"completed"}}
