{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_62","type":"mcp_tool_call","server":"fetch","tool":"fetch","arguments":{"max_length":10000,"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/China_and_the_United_Nations"},"result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Contents of https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/China_and_the_United_Nations:\n[People's Republic of China](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/China \"China\")\n\n|  |  |\n| --- | --- |\n|  | |\n| [United Nations](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/United_Nations \"United Nations\") [membership](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Member_states_of_the_United_Nations \"Member states of the United Nations\") | |\n| Represented by | * [National Government](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nationalist_government \"Nationalist government\") of the [Republic of China](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Republic_of_China_(1912%E2%80%931949) \"Republic of China (1912–1949)\") (1945–1948) * [Constitutional](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Constitution_of_the_Republic_of_China \"Constitution of the Republic of China\") [Government of the Republic of China](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Government_of_the_Republic_of_China \"Government of the Republic of China\") (1948–[1949](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Retreat_of_the_government_of_the_Republic_of_China_to_Taiwan \"Retreat of the government of the Republic of China to Taiwan\")) * [Constitutional](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Constitution_of_the_Republic_of_China \"Constitution of the Republic of China\") [Government of the Republic of China](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Government_of_the_Republic_of_China \"Government of the Republic of China\") on [Taiwan](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Taiwan \"Taiwan\") (1949–1971) * [Central People's Government](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/State_Council_of_the_People's_Republic_of_China \"State Council of the People's Republic of China\") of the [People's Republic of China](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Government_of_China \"Government of China\") (1971–present) |\n| Membership | Full member |\n| Since | 24 October 1945 |\n| [UNSC](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/United_Nations_Security_Council \"United Nations Security Council\") seat | [Permanent](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Permanent_members_of_the_United_Nations_Security_Council \"Permanent members of the United Nations Security Council\") |\n| [Permanent Representative](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Permanent_Representative_of_China_to_the_United_Nations \"Permanent Representative of China to the United Nations\") | [Fu Cong](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fu_Cong \"Fu Cong\") |\n\nThe People's Republic of China is one of the [members](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Member_states_of_the_United_Nations \"Member states of the United Nations\") of the [United Nations](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/United_Nations \"United Nations\") and is one of five [permanent members](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Permanent_members_of_the_United_Nations_Security_Council \"Permanent members of the United Nations Security Council\") of its [Security Council](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/United_Nations_Security_Council \"United Nations Security Council\"). The Republic of China was one of the victorious [Allies](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Allies_of_World_War_II \"Allies of World War II\") of [World War II](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/World_War_II \"World War II\") (the Chinese theatre of which was the [Second Sino-Japanese War](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Second_Sino-Japanese_War \"Second Sino-Japanese War\")), they joined the UN as one of its founding member countries in 1945. The subsequent resumption of the [Chinese Civil War](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chinese_Civil_War \"Chinese Civil War\") between the government of Republic of China and the rebel forces of the Chinese Communist Party, led to the latter's victory on the mainland and the [establishment of the People's Republic of China](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Proclamation_of_the_People's_Republic_of_China \"Proclamation of the People's Republic of China\") (PRC) in 1949. Nearly all of [mainland China](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mainland_China \"Mainland China\") was soon under its control[[note 1]](#cite_note-1) and the ROC government (then referred to in the West as \"Nationalist China\") [retreated](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Retreat_of_the_government_of_the_Republic_of_China_to_Taiwan \"Retreat of the government of the Republic of China to Taiwan\") to the [island of Taiwan](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Geography_of_Taiwan \"Geography of Taiwan\").\n\nThe [One-China policy](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/One-China_policy \"One-China policy\") advocated by both governments[[1]](#cite_note-:5-2) dismantled the solution of dual representation but, amid the [Cold War](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cold_War \"Cold War\") and [Korean War](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Korean_War \"Korean War\"), the United States and its allies opposed the replacement of the ROC at the United Nations until 1971, although they were persuaded to pressure the government of the ROC to accept international recognition of [Mongolia](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mongolian_People's_Republic \"Mongolian People's Republic\")'s independence in 1961. The PRC sought to be recognized by the United Nations from the 1950s,[[2]](#cite_note-3) but the United States managed to keep the PRC out of the UN until 1971. The [General Assembly Resolution 1668](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/United_Nations_General_Assembly_Resolution_1668 \"United Nations General Assembly Resolution 1668\") which demanded a majority of two thirds for the recognition of new members was adopted[[3]](#cite_note-4) in 1961. Canada and other allies of the United States individually shifted their recognitions of China to the PRC, which the US opposed.[[4]](#cite_note-:7-5) Some attempted to recognize both Chinas separately, which both Chinas opposed, each declaring itself the only legitimate representative of China.[[4]](#cite_note-:7-5) Annual motions to replace the ROC with the PRC were introduced first by the Soviet Union, then India and also Albania, but these were defeated.[[4]](#cite_note-:7-5)\n\nAmid the [Sino-Soviet split](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sino-Soviet_split \"Sino-Soviet split\") and [Vietnam War](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vietnam_War \"Vietnam War\"), the current President of the United States at the time, [Richard Nixon](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Richard_Nixon \"Richard Nixon\"), entered into negotiations with [Chinese Communist Party Chairman](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chairman_of_the_Chinese_Communist_Party \"Chairman of the Chinese Communist Party\") [Mao Zedong](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mao_Zedong \"Mao Zedong\"), initially through a secret 1971 trip undertaken by [Henry Kissinger](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Henry_Kissinger \"Henry Kissinger\") to visit [Zhou Enlai](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zhou_Enlai \"Zhou Enlai\"). On 25 October 1971, a motion to recognize the People's Republic of China as the sole legal China, initiated by 17 UN members led by Albania, was passed as [General Assembly Resolution 2758](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/United_Nations_General_Assembly_Resolution_2758 \"United Nations General Assembly Resolution 2758\"). It was supported by most of the [communist states](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Communist_state \"Communist state\") (including the [Soviet Union](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Soviet_Union \"Soviet Union\")) and [non-aligned countries](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Non-Aligned_Movement \"Non-Aligned Movement\") (such as [India](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/India \"India\")), but also by some [NATO](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/NATO \"NATO\") countries, such as the United Kingdom and Italy. After the [PRC was seated](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Accession_of_the_People's_Republic_of_China_to_the_United_Nations \"Accession of the People's Republic of China to the United Nations\") on 15 November 1971, Nixon [personally visited mainland China](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1972_Nixon_visit_to_China \"1972 Nixon visit to China\") the next year, beginning the normalization of [PRC–USA relations](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/China%E2%80%93United_States_relations \"China–United States relations\"). The Republic of China maintained the view it was the sole legitimate representative of China until 1988, but eventually turned to a foreign policy which sought international recognition through a so-called [checkbook diplomacy](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Checkbook_diplomacy \"Checkbook diplomacy\").[[1]](#cite_note-:5-2) These moves have been opposed and mostly blocked by the People's Republic of China, forcing the Republic of China to join international organizations under other names, including \"[Chinese Taipei](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chinese_Taipei \"Chinese Taipei\")\" at the [International Olympic Committee](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/International_Olympic_Committee \"International Olympic Committee\").\n\nThe Republic of China's most recent request for admission was turned down in 2007,[[5]](#cite_note-6) but a number of European governments—led by the United States—protested to the UN's [Office of Legal Affairs](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/United_Nations_Office_of_Legal_Affairs \"United Nations Office of Legal Affairs\") to force the global body and its secretary-general to stop using the reference \"Taiwan is a part of China\".[[6]](#cite_note-7)\n\n[![](//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0a/Chiang_Kai-shek_ratified_the_Charter_of_the_United_Nations_19450824.jpg/250px-Chiang_Kai-shek_ratified_the_Charter_of_the_United_Nations_19450824.jpg)](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Chiang_Kai-shek_ratified_the_Charter_of_the_United_Nations_19450824.jpg)\n\nChina was honored for its long struggle on [the War of Resistance against Axis Power](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Second_Sino-Japanese_War \"Second Sino-Japanese War\") since [Japanese aggression in Northeast China](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Japanese_invasion_of_Manchuria \"Japanese invasion of Manchuria\") as the first signatory to affix the [United Nations Charter](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/United_Nations_Charter \"United Nations Charter\") on 24 August 1945. [Generalissimo](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Generalissimo \"Generalissimo\") [Chiang Kai-shek](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chiang_Kai-shek \"Chiang Kai-shek\") was the representative of the [Republic of \n\n<error>Content truncated. Call the fetch tool with a start_index of 10000 to get more content.</error>"}],"structured_content":null},"error":null,"status":"completed"}}
