{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_65","type":"mcp_tool_call","server":"fetch","tool":"fetch","arguments":{"max_length":8000,"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/South_China_Sea_disputes"},"result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Contents of https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/South_China_Sea_disputes:\n[![](//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4a/South_China_Sea_vector.svg/250px-South_China_Sea_vector.svg.png)](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:South_China_Sea_vector.svg)\n\nMap of the [nine-dash line](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nine-dash_line \"Nine-dash line\") and EEZs\n\n[Brunei](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brunei \"Brunei\"), [Indonesia](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Indonesia \"Indonesia\"), [Malaysia](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Malaysia \"Malaysia\"), the [Philippines](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Philippines \"Philippines\"), the [People's Republic of China](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/People's_Republic_of_China \"People's Republic of China\") (PRC), [Taiwan](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Taiwan \"Taiwan\") (Republic of China/ROC), and [Vietnam](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vietnam \"Vietnam\") have conflicting island and maritime claims in the [South China Sea](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/South_China_Sea \"South China Sea\"). The disputes involve the islands, reefs, banks, and other features of the region, including the [Spratly Islands](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spratly_Islands \"Spratly Islands\"), [Paracel Islands](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paracel_Islands \"Paracel Islands\"), [Scarborough Shoal](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Scarborough_Shoal \"Scarborough Shoal\"), and some boundaries in the [Gulf of Tonkin](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gulf_of_Tonkin \"Gulf of Tonkin\"). The waters near the Indonesian [Natuna Islands](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Natuna_Islands \"Natuna Islands\"), which some regard as geographically part of the South China Sea, are disputed as well.\n\nAn estimated US$3.36 trillion worth of [global trade](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/International_trade \"International trade\") passes through the South China Sea annually,[[1]](#cite_note-China_Power-2017-1) which accounts for a third of the global maritime trade.[[2]](#cite_note-2) 80 percent of China's energy imports and 40 percent of China's total trade passes through the South China Sea.[[1]](#cite_note-China_Power-2017-1) Claimant states are interested in retaining or acquiring the rights to fishing stocks, the exploration and potential exploitation of [crude oil](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crude_oil \"Crude oil\") and [natural gas](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Natural_gas \"Natural gas\") in the seabed of various parts of the South China Sea, and the strategic control of important [shipping lanes](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shipping_lanes \"Shipping lanes\"). [Maritime security](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Maritime_security \"Maritime security\") is also an issue, as the ongoing disputes present challenges for shipping.[[3]](#cite_note-3)\n\nAccording to researchers, claims to any of the features were not seriously made until the 19th or the early 20th century.[[4]](#cite_note-:1-4)[[5]](#cite_note-:2a-5) The Paracel Islands, currently occupied by China, are contested by Taiwan and Vietnam. The Spratly Islands are claimed by all three, where Vietnam occupies the greatest number of features and Taiwan occupies the largest, [Taiping Island](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Taiping_Island \"Taiping Island\"). Brunei, Malaysia, and the Philippines also claim some of the features in the island chain.[[6]](#cite_note-:0-6) By the 1970s, the Philippines, Taiwan, and Vietnam had militarily occupied one or more of the Spratly Islands.[[7]](#cite_note-7) By 2015, the PRC had established 8 outposts, Malaysia 5, the Philippines 8, Taiwan 1, and Vietnam 48.[[8]](#cite_note-8)\n\nFor decades, the Philippines and Vietnam were the most active in building [artificial islands](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Artificial_island \"Artificial island\") in the area,[[9]](#cite_note-9)[[10]](#cite_note-10) but from 2014 to 2016 China's construction activity outpaced them.[[11]](#cite_note-Asia_Maritime_Transparency_Initiative-11) By 2023, China had reclaimed around five square miles with its artificial islands, at least one of which housed military equipment.[[12]](#cite_note-12)[[6]](#cite_note-:0-6)\n\nChina's actions in the South China Sea have been criticized as part of its \"[salami slicing](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chinese_salami_slicing_strategy \"Chinese salami slicing strategy\")\"/\"[cabbage wrapping](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cabbage_tactics \"Cabbage tactics\")\" strategies.[[13]](#cite_note-13)[[14]](#cite_note-14) Since 2015, the United States and other states such as [France](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/France \"France\") and the [United Kingdom](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/United_Kingdom \"United Kingdom\") have conducted [freedom of navigation operations](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Freedom_of_navigation \"Freedom of navigation\") (FONOP) in the region.[[15]](#cite_note-15) A 2016 [arbitration tribunal](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/South_China_Sea_Arbitration \"South China Sea Arbitration\"), without determining the sovereignty of any of the islands, concluded that China lacks historical titles to the maritime areas within the [nine-dash line](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nine-dash_line \"Nine-dash line\"). The ruling was rejected by both the PRC and ROC.\n\n## Disputes in the South China Sea region\n\n[[edit](/w/index.php?title=Territorial_disputes_in_the_South_China_Sea&action=edit&section=1 \"Edit section: Disputes in the South China Sea region\")]\n\nSummary of disputes\n\n| Area of dispute | Brunei | China | Indonesia | Malaysia | Philippines | Taiwan | Vietnam |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| The [nine-dash line](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nine-dash_line \"Nine-dash line\") | ✔ | ✔ | ✔ | ✔ | ✔ | ✔ | ✔ |\n| Vietnamese coast |  | ✔ |  |  |  | ✔ | ✔ |\n| Sea area north of Borneo | ✔ | ✔ |  | ✔ | ✔ | ✔ |  |\n| South China Sea islands |  | ✔ |  | ✔ | ✔ | ✔ | ✔ |\n| Sea area north of the Natuna Islands |  | ✔ | ✔ |  |  | ✔ |  |\n| Sea area west of Palawan and Luzon |  | ✔ |  |  | ✔ | ✔ |  |\n| Sabah area |  |  | ✔ | ✔ | ✔ |  |  |\n| Luzon Strait |  | ✔ |  |  | ✔ | ✔ |  |\n| Taiwan and China |  | ✔ |  |  |  | ✔ |  |\n\n[![Map](https://maps.wikimedia.org/img/osm,6,9,114,500x375.png?lang=en)](/wiki/Special:Map/6/9/114/en)\n\n[![About OpenStreetMaps](//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/Transparent.svg/20px-Transparent.svg.png)](https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright \"About OpenStreetMaps\")\n\n[![Maps: terms of use](//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/Transparent.svg/20px-Transparent.svg.png)](https://foundation.wikimedia.org/wiki/Policy:Maps_Terms_of_Use \"Maps: terms of use\")\n\n140km  \n87miles\n\nS\n\nO\n\nU\n\nT\n\nH\n\nC\n\nH\n\nI\n\nN\n\nA\n\nS\n\nE\n\nA\n\nD\n\na\n\nn\n\ng\n\ne\n\nr\n\no\n\nu\n\ns\n\nG\n\nr\n\no\n\nu\n\nn\n\nd\n\n![Louisa Reef](//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9d/Yellow_pog.svg/20px-Yellow_pog.svg.png)\n\n56\n\n[![Louisa Reef](//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/02/Transparent_square.svg/20px-Transparent_square.svg.png)](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Louisa_Reef \"Louisa Reef\")\n\n[![Louisa Reef](//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/02/Transparent_square.svg/20px-Transparent_square.svg.png)](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Louisa_Reef \"Louisa Reef\")\n\n![Mariveles Reef](//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ab/Green_pog.svg/20px-Green_pog.svg.png)\n\n55\n\n[![Mariveles Reef](//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/02/Transparent_square.svg/20px-Transparent_square.svg.png)](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mariveles_Reef \"Mariveles Reef\")\n\n[![Mariveles Reef](//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/02/Transparent_square.svg/20px-Transparent_square.svg.png)](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mariveles_Reef \"Mariveles Reef\")\n\n![Investigator Shoal](//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ab/Green_pog.svg/20px-Green_pog.svg.png)\n\n54\n\n[![Investigator Shoal](//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/02/Transparent_square.svg/20px-Transparent_square.svg.png)](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Investigator_Shoal \"Investigator Shoal\")\n\n[![Investigator Shoal](//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/02/Transparent_square.svg/20px-Transparent_square.svg.png)](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Investigator_Shoal \"Investigator Shoal\")\n\n![Erica Reef](//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ab/Green_pog.svg/20px-Green_pog.svg.png)\n\n53\n\n[![Erica \n\n<error>Content truncated. Call the fetch tool with a start_index of 8000 to get more content.</error>"}],"structured_content":null},"error":null,"status":"completed"}}
