{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_76","type":"mcp_tool_call","server":"fetch","tool":"fetch","arguments":{"max_length":8000,"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/China_under_Xi_Jinping"},"result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Contents of https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/China_under_Xi_Jinping:\n| New Era of Socialism with Chinese Characteristics | |\n| --- | --- |\n| 2012–present | |\n| |  |  | | --- | --- | | [History of China (2002–2012)](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/History_of_China_(2002%E2%80%932012) \"History of China (2002–2012)\") |  | | |\n| Xi Jinping in 2026 | |\n| Location | [People's Republic of China](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/China \"China\") |\n| [CCP General Secretary](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/General_Secretary_of_the_Chinese_Communist_Party \"General Secretary of the Chinese Communist Party\") | [Xi Jinping](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Xi_Jinping \"Xi Jinping\") |\n| President | Xi Jinping |\n| Prime Minister(s) | [Li Keqiang](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Li_Keqiang \"Li Keqiang\") [Li Qiang](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Li_Qiang \"Li Qiang\") |\n| Key events | [Anti-corruption campaign](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anti-corruption_campaign_under_Xi_Jinping \"Anti-corruption campaign under Xi Jinping\") [Battle against poverty](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_against_poverty \"Battle against poverty\") [China–United States trade war](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/China%E2%80%93United_States_trade_war \"China–United States trade war\") [2019–2020 Hong Kong protests](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2019%E2%80%932020_Hong_Kong_protests \"2019–2020 Hong Kong protests\") [COVID-19 pandemic](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/COVID-19_pandemic_in_China \"COVID-19 pandemic in China\") [2022 Winter Olympics](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2022_Winter_Olympics \"2022 Winter Olympics\") |\n\nSince 2012, the [People's Republic of China](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/People's_Republic_of_China \"People's Republic of China\") has officially referred to its present era as the **New Era of Socialism with Chinese Characteristics**, which started when [Xi Jinping](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Xi_Jinping \"Xi Jinping\") succeeded [Hu Jintao](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hu_Jintao \"Hu Jintao\") as [general secretary](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/General_Secretary_of_the_Chinese_Communist_Party \"General Secretary of the Chinese Communist Party\") of the [Chinese Communist Party](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chinese_Communist_Party \"Chinese Communist Party\") (CCP) following the [18th National Congress of the Chinese Communist Party](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/18th_National_Congress_of_the_Chinese_Communist_Party \"18th National Congress of the Chinese Communist Party\"). In 2016, Xi was proclaimed the CCP's fourth [leadership core](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Leadership_core \"Leadership core\"), following [Mao Zedong](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mao_Zedong \"Mao Zedong\"), [Deng Xiaoping](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Deng_Xiaoping \"Deng Xiaoping\"), and [Jiang Zemin](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jiang_Zemin \"Jiang Zemin\").\n\nWhile overseeing China's domestic policy, Xi has introduced far-ranging measures to enforce party discipline and strengthen internal unity. His [anti-corruption campaign](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anti-corruption_campaign_under_Xi_Jinping \"Anti-corruption campaign under Xi Jinping\") led to the downfall of prominent incumbent and retired CCP officials, including former PSC member [Zhou Yongkang](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zhou_Yongkang \"Zhou Yongkang\"). For the sake of promoting \"[common prosperity](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Common_prosperity \"Common prosperity\")\", Under Xi, China has enacted a series of policies designed to increase equality, overseen [targeted poverty alleviation](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Targeted_Poverty_Alleviation \"Targeted Poverty Alleviation\") programs as part of the [battle against poverty](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_against_poverty \"Battle against poverty\"), and directed a broad crackdown in 2021 against the tech sector, as well as drastically curtailing the tutoring industry and reducing homework burdens. Furthermore, China has expanded support for [state-owned enterprises](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/State-owned_enterprises_of_China \"State-owned enterprises of China\") (SOEs), emphasized advanced manufacturing and tech development, advanced [military-civil fusion](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Military-civil_fusion \"Military-civil fusion\"), and attempted to reform the country's property sector. Following the onset of the [COVID-19 pandemic in mainland China](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/COVID-19_pandemic_in_mainland_China \"COVID-19 pandemic in mainland China\"), the country initially responded with a [zero-COVID](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zero-COVID \"Zero-COVID\") policy from January 2020 to December 2022 before ultimately shifting towards a mitigation strategy after widespread [protests](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2022_COVID-19_protests_in_China \"2022 COVID-19 protests in China\") occurred. In foreign policy, Xi emphasizes the [Community of Common Destiny](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Community_of_Common_Destiny \"Community of Common Destiny\"). He seeks to increase China's ability to shape international norms in emerging policy areas (described as \"new frontiers\") like space and the internet, where China can position itself as an early entrant. Xi also seeks to increase China's discourse power, which he frames as China's \"right to speak.\" Since Xi came to power, China has pursued a more hardline foreign policy particularly with regard to [China's relations with the United States](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/China%E2%80%93United_States_relations \"China–United States relations\"), the [nine-dash line](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nine-dash_line \"Nine-dash line\") in the [South China Sea](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Territorial_disputes_in_the_South_China_Sea \"Territorial disputes in the South China Sea\"), and the [Sino-Indian border dispute](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sino-Indian_border_dispute \"Sino-Indian border dispute\"). Additionally, for the sake of advancing Chinese economic interests abroad, China has sought to expand its influence in Africa and Eurasia by championing the [Belt and Road Initiative](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Belt_and_Road_Initiative \"Belt and Road Initiative\").\n\nRelations between Beijing and Taipei deteriorated under Taiwanese president [Tsai Ing-wen](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tsai_Ing-wen \"Tsai Ing-wen\"), successor of [Ma Ying-jeou](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ma_Ying-jeou \"Ma Ying-jeou\") whom Xi [met](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/First_Ma%E2%80%93Xi_meeting \"First Ma–Xi meeting\") in 2015. In 2020, a [national security law in Hong Kong](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2020_Hong_Kong_national_security_law \"2020 Hong Kong national security law\") was passed, which clamped down on political opposition in the city, especially [pro-democracy activists](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pro-democracy_camp_(Hong_Kong) \"Pro-democracy camp (Hong Kong)\"). Since Xi came to power, China has witnessed a significant increase in [censorship](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Censorship_in_China \"Censorship in China\") and [mass surveillance](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mass_surveillance_in_China \"Mass surveillance in China\"), a deterioration in [human rights](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Human_rights_in_China \"Human rights in China\") (including the [persecution of Uyghurs](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Persecution_of_Uyghurs_in_China \"Persecution of Uyghurs in China\")), the rise of a [cult of personality](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Xi_Jinping's_cult_of_personality \"Xi Jinping's cult of personality\"), the [removal](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2018_amendment_to_the_Constitution_of_China \"2018 amendment to the Constitution of China\") of [term limits](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Term_limits \"Term limits\") for the presidency in 2018, as well as an increased role for the CCP in society. Xi's political ideas and principles, known as [Xi Jinping Thought](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Xi_Jinping_Thought \"Xi Jinping Thought\"), have been incorporated into the [party](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Constitution_of_the_Chinese_Communist_Party \"Constitution of the Chinese Commu\n\n<error>Content truncated. Call the fetch tool with a start_index of 8000 to get more content.</error>"}],"structured_content":null},"error":null,"status":"completed"}}
