-04 (local-prior)** — *LF004.* `local-prior:2B.1`. **Claim:** 4.95% of government spending. **Lenses:** 2B.8.\n- **E2B-05** — **Canonical key:** sipri.org_2404_fs_milex_2023::china-296b-2023. **Locator:** SIPRI Fact Sheet \"Trends in World Military Expenditure, 2023\" (April 2024), p.1 reference text via Google snippet. **Source type/confidence:** high (SIPRI). **Claim:** \"China, the world's second largest military spender, allocated an estimated $296 billion to the military in 2023, an increase of 6.0 per cent.\" **Period fit:** exact 2023. **Role:** corroborates local priors; contextual for 2B.8. **Lenses:** 2B.8.\n- **E2B-06** — **Canonical key:** en.wikipedia.org/wiki/China%E2%80%93Russia_relations::russia-2025-trade-234b-context. **Locator:** Wikipedia \"China–Russia relations\" (lead/early body): \"The annual trade between China and Russia was US$234 billion as of 2025.\" With prior-year trajectory establishing deep 2023 trade relationship. **Source type/confidence:** medium_high. **Claim:** Deep economic ties with Russia, sanctions-impacted trade continues; Beijing's posture on NATO enlargement opposed. **Period fit:** 2023 baseline. **Role:** contextual for 2B.2 (no initiation of war) and 2B.5 (proxy/ally conduct). **Lenses:** 2B.5, 2B.6.\n- **E2B-07** — **Canonical key:** en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2023_in_China::south-china-sea-nov-2023-philippines. **Locator:** Wikipedia \"2023 in China,\" 10 November 2023. **Claim:** \"China imposes 'control measures' against Philippine vessels at a contested South China Sea location after a Philippine auxiliary ship entered the area which China deemed as infringing on its sovereignty.\" **Period fit:** exact 2023. **Role:** negative (coercive cross-border action). **Lenses:** 2B.2, 2B.4, 2B.7.\n- **E2B-08** — **Canonical key:** en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2023_in_China::assad-visit-22-sept-2023. **Locator:** Wikipedia \"2023 in China,\" 22 September 2023. **Claim:** \"Syrian President Bashar al-Assad visits China, meets with Chin